.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH taur-verify-user 1  "taur-verify-user " 
.SH NAME
taur\-verify\-user \- Mark an account\*(Aqs email as verified (admin)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtaur verify\-user\fR [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fINAME\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Mark an account\*(Aqs email as verified (admin)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<HOME>\fR
Data directory (default: ~/.local/share/taur)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_HOME\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fINAME\fR>

.SH ENVIRONMENT
Command\-line flags take precedence over environment variables, which take precedence over defaults.
.TP
\fBTAUR_HOME\fR
Data directory (database, git repos, outbox, SSH host key). Default: ~/.local/share/taur.
